        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0561" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1318</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Gustavo Caballero, former governor of Camaguey, was seriously wounded and
                    150 of his followers taken prisoners by Colonel Pujol today. Caballero has been
                    operating between Camaguey and Manatí in Oriente. In an encounter three days ago
                    40 of his men were killed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
